From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE, _ABSORB_VEC, _KVB8

ai-engine 436970264 grafted onto the pin stack. MLA_FUSEMERGE fuses a chunk pass that
stops at its last live key tile with a merge that walks the row's chunks in registers;
ABSORB_VEC reads bf16 kv_b by 16-byte loads; KVB8 reads E4M3 kv_b a 128-wide load times
its scale. glm_glue_attn_ovn.cuh and glm_glue_latent_ovn.cuh carry the kernels, glue.Mla
reads the knobs at load and glue.Set carries the choice, cuda_latent.fuses picks the
fused path, and the DSA block routes through it. Default off: today's chunk programs
and merge.

Pin adaptations, each forced by the pin's own shapes: Mla.read/wanted are restored on the
pin's struct (the conflict had dropped them) with the knob set the pin actually has;
Kernels gains the new function fields and the load loop takes the source's
skipped-kernel form so unset ones carry a null handle; Set keeps the pin's fields plus
.mla; cuda_latent's headBlock takes rows alone at the pin; expandV takes `sv` at the pin
so the DSA call passes it. Comment lines single-lined.

Gates on pin+0001..0021: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins 226/226 green.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0039: the kernel loop skips fields that are not plain functions
- 0057: the one-pass base check, which calls the glue.Kernels.loadOvn this patch adds

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE, _ABSORB_VEC and _KVB8 have their rows from onepass-pipe, where the fold first reads them (fold-series.md J20); Mla.wanted() takes this patch's two-knob form (KVB8 counts on Kernels.wanted, in glue-fuse).
- glm_glue_attn_ovn.cuh and glm_glue_latent_ovn.cuh are ours and apply unchanged. 42735f94f moved glm_attn's chunk bodies into common/mla.cuh with RW and SPLIT template parameters whose defaults are GLM's own instantiation (the commit keeps glm_glue's bytes), so the OVN copies still mirror the default body; glm_glue_attn.cuh still includes common/mla.cuh, so glm_attn:: stays in scope. nvcc is the gate (no local build of the .cuh).
- glm-onepass-exact-check joins glm_ovn_checks.zig.
- source: work/fold/0025-mla-knobs.patch

Boot fix, 2026-11-12 (docs/audit-2026-11-12/mla-boot-fix.md): tf_glm_chunks_16_fp8_skip and
tf_glm_chunks_32_fp8_skip came from the fork with its FP8-on-pages parameter list (16 parameters, ending pt and
pstep), while latent.chunks passes an E4M3 entry the 14 arguments tf_glm_chunks_*_fp8 take, so the launch read two
argument slots the host never wrote and a TF_GLM_OVN_MLA_FUSEMERGE=1 boot with an FP8 latent cache failed with
CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE on tf_glm_chunks_32_fp8_skip. Shared memory was never short: every chunk entry needs
wide_smem<HB>() (83,328 or 101,120 bytes, no static shared) and gets exactly that as attribute and launch size.
Fixed here: both entries take tf_glm_chunks_*_fp8's list, tf_glm_chunks_32_fp8_fused takes no page table either and
fused() passes pt and pstep to the BF16 form only and refuses FP8 on pages as chunks() does, the fork's FP8 page
branch is out of glm_attn_ovn::chunks (its FP8 fetch is now chunks_wide's slab-only one), static_asserts tie each
bounded entry's parameters to its default form's (nvcc fails on the old lists), and glm-mla-skip-check runs the
bounded and fused launches against today's chunk programs and merge, byte for byte, on BF16 and FP8 caches.

